nd for Croatia as a tourist  country which  is also an automobile destination to a  great extent that will mean a lot the  fact that we are joining the Eurozone is  another signal to all those coming to  Croatia how welcome they are and this  simplifies their selection of Croatia  as a holiday venue and the selections  are what we do I would also like to  thank the Ministers of the interior of  Foreign Affairs of Finance all members  of the government current and the former  who all contributed to bringing us here  into the deepest integration that we can  belong to 31 years ago we were not  internationally recognized and in only  three decades  since the Liberation over the  temporarily occupied territories of  Croatia for which I now give the  Gratitude again to Croatian War veteran  veterans and without their contribution  we wouldn't have had a state and since  our joining the Union in 2013 and these  two huge steps which have brought us in  the group of 15 countries that belonged  to both Schengen and the Eurozone and  this brings us to the achievement of the  goal defined by the first Croatian  president Dr  franojiman Who's one of the program  points this was Croatia's full-joining  of Europe these processes are now  concluded and the delivery every year  actually also saw the opening of the  parachutes bridge this is a sovereign  mover and we enjoyed the support  of the European Union  357 million euros plus the contribution  of Croatia the participation of  Slovenian Architects this is a wonderful  combination indeed and this is a year in  which we endured all pressures that were  the consequences of the pandemic of the  global crisis  caused by the Russian aggression against  Ukraine we sought solutions for all  pressures energy inflatory and others I  would also like to thank the Croatian  police for having guarded Croatian  borders and I am very happy that now  Croatia can now dedicate its capacities  to the external borders the Schengen  borders 350 kilometers with Serbia  Bosnia and Montenegro without any wires  wire fences or barriers these are the  political principles that we adhere to  and we are very happy that in the past  year Muslim Herzegovina became a  candidate the country and we will not be  separated by barriers or wires we shall  help the Schengen gets stronger we shall  help  bring the euro in and make it become  even more stronger and I would like to  thank the president and the commission I  would like to thank Slovenia former  president Mr pahar and  prime minister golub former Minister  yansha all of them contributed to  Croatia's attainment of these goals  that and I thank all other member states  who gave us their positive vote and they  thank the European Parliament  I'm proud today  thank you prime minister blenkovich now  we give the flow to the president of the  commission Mrs Wonderland prime minister  Madam president Natasha first of all  happy New Year  to the two of you and to everybody here  around us I'm delighted to be with you  here today it is a day to celebrate  it is the season of new beginnings the  1st of January  new chapters that are being opened and  there is no place in Europe whether it  is more true today that it is the season  of new beginnings and new chapters than  here  the border between Croatia and Slovenia  today Croatia joins the Schengen area  and the Eurozone  to immense achievements for the youngest  member  state of the European Union and both  reached on the very same day  so indeed this is a day for the history  books  but above all this is a day of joy and  pride for the creation people  it is testimony of your amazing journey  your hard work and your determination  it is a day of Celebration not only for  Creations but for all European citizens  and from now on internal internal  borders can be crossed freely without  controls like he and bregana and all the  other Crossing points at land with  Slovenia and Hungary at Sea with Italy  and as of March by air with all other  Schengen States  no more checks no more passport controls  no more cues  just people crossing smoothly as we can  see right behind us  tourists visiting Croatia will no longer  need a separate Visa  they can visit with the same Schengen  visa as they use to travel to all other  Schengen countries  the next generation of Creations will  grow up in Schengen  people will be able to travel freely  business will be unhindered by checks  seamless travel will bring tangible  results  for people living along the border  working across the border or having  family on both sides of the Border  communities will grow closer together  and your presence here today Madam  president  clearly shows how important this day is  not just for Croatia but also for all  its neighbors  we will need to work very closely  together to protect Schengen and  preserve its benefits because indeed  Schengen cannot be taken for granted  its functioning has been challenged over  time and it continues to be challenged  Schengen is about commitment  and mutual Trust  in Schengen we rely on each other  and we know that we can trust you  and that we can rely on Croatia  being able to cross internal borders  without controls is one important  achievement  being able to pay cross-borders using  the same EU currency is another one  and I know by my own personal experience  that creations will always remember the  first time they paid with euros  the first time they held the Euro coin  minted with your national emblem the  Kuna  as a symbol of the successful Union  between your national identity and your  European destiny  today you are joining a community of  347 million Europeans  who are using the euro in their everyday  lives  the Euro makes us stronger at home  it facilitates Investments and trade  across borders  thus making our economy more vibrant  it helps to create jobs it brings  macroeconomic stability and credibility  and as the second most important  currency globally  the Euro also makes us stronger on the  world stage  indeed the euro is one of our best  Collective achievements and it is of  course much more than a currency  it is a token of unity  Beyond borders and Beyond languages  Deandre  what an extraordinary success for the  people of Croatia  I know how hard you worked for this day  to come congratulations again  to join the Euro and Schengen  communities just 10 years after Croatia  joined the European Union  this is a day of great pride  of great emotion  and thank you very much for inviting me  to be part of this thank you very much  thank you Mrs fonderlein I now invite  Mrs pets Musa  I also welcome all of you  madam president Mr Prime Minister  I welcome all of you here and this is  indeed my first visit as the president  of Croatia this is a gift to Europe  and it's wonderful to be here with our  neighbors I would like to congratulate  all  Croatian citizens for having joined the  Schengen area and the Eurozone I  congratulate the Croatian government we  know that this was not an easy path and  easy trajectory Mr blinkovich you  deserve to be congratulated for these  achievements and everyone in Croatia can  really be proud of this path that  Croatia has traveled  Madam president of the commission you  also were very attentive to this  process and you encourage others to join  the European Union I as the president of  Slovenia have a full faith in the united  Europe sometimes we may see things  differently but integration is the only  way for the states of Western Balkans  I'm sure that I shall continue the  Slovenian  tradition of assisting States  in the neighborhood to join the  Integrations together with prime  minister blankovich and milanovic and I  would like to say that this is also a  message a message that Europe is our  home and I am convinced that it will  stay so for a very long time it is Our  obligation to defend it to make it a  pleasant for living  in order for us to be equal members of  the great European integration let us  look back  we all know in Slovenia that Primos  truber who founded protestantism in my  country the father of Croatia of  Slovenian literacy we know of that  figure but it is not so well known that  he  helped a great deal to publish and print  books in Croatian in the 16th century  these books were printed in Germany  symbolically this is a connection  between  who helped print and publish books in  Croatian and he was the one who  overcame borders and was led by the idea  of reformation  and we are  led by the idea of United Europe and our  common history can bring us together all  separators and we are the ones who  choose which course to take and I'm  certain that history can only bring us  together bring us closer because  separation  happened all too often in this area in  former Yugoslavia I used to work in  Croatia  and there was in this border that time  as a president of Slovenia I am so happy  on this historical date when Croatia and  Slovenia have no borders between  themselves anymore and when the border  is opened and  it really gives me joy and I am sure  this means a lot no not only  for the Nationals of Slovenia and  Croatia  but um  Slovenian citizens come here for  holidays over a million of them every  year but also it's a two-way street the  croats go to Slovenia to ski in the  winter and uh also work and study in my  country and I said at the very beginning  that this is a great moment for croats  and but it is also a great step for  Slovenia and its Nationals and for my  homeland it is a holiday for them as  well  Mr blankovich my sincere gratitude goes  to you for having invited me to be a  part of this wonderful event at the  border between Croatia and Slovenia and  bregana have become one and I would like  to visit your present Mr milanovic in  future  and um  I would like to ask to draw this path  further  thank you that is all for the media  [Music]

